{
  "stage": "S3",
  "protocol": {
    "hypothesis": "A store leak, and the uneaten food of ghost learners, shows only at a count. Counting every 10 or 5 school days instead of 20 catches them sooner. A slow leak then leaves a smaller gap at each count, so the shortfall listing also uses the sum of the gaps over the last 20 school days (same threshold of 2 days of food); more counts also give honest count errors more chances to trip it.\n",
    "change": "Data: counts every 10 and every 5 school days (seeds 8101-8115, compared with the same seeds at 20). Ranking: a school is listed first if a count in the week, or the sum of its counts' gaps over the last 20 school days, is more than 2 days of food short. The summed rule is also run at 20 days. This is a programme procedure plus a ranking rule, reported as system design, never as a model gain.\n"
  },
